      "rules_subdir": "javascript",
      "source_path": "javascript/ql/test/query-tests/Security/CWE-078/CommandInjection",
      "alert_query": "$ Alert",
      "expected": {
        "alert_lines": 96,
        "alert_lines_covered": 11,
        "good_lines": 0,
        "good_lines_reported": 0
      },
      "promotion_ready": false,
      "promotion_blocker": "The 96 alert lines are the whole CodeQL command injection tree, which is dominated by sinks these rules never claimed: execa, cross-spawn, ssh2, opener, @actions/exec, promisified exec wrappers, and spawn or execFile argument arrays. 11 alert lines are inside the published scope of cra-javascript-exec-injection, exec or execSync resolved from child_process with the command built by concatenation or template interpolation, and all 11 are covered. Read the covered figure against that 11, not against 96. The tree carries no good-marked lines, so this benchmark measures recall only and gives no false positive signal."
    },
